     1,
     "<div><font color=\"#333333\" face=\"Menlo, Monaco, Consolas, Courier New, monospace\"><span style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap\">Does geom/stat_bin2d generate an intermediate data matrix from the xy data it is fed?  If so can this matrix be extracted?  If the matrix can&#39;t be extracted, which function is bin2d using to do the binning?</span></font></div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><br></span></div><div>I assumed I would find the binned data in &quot;d&quot;:</div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><br></span></div>d &lt;- ggplot(diamonds, aes(x = x, y = y)) + xlim(4,10) + ylim(4,10) + geom_bin2d()</span><div><span style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace\">str(d)</span><br></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace\">But I do not see it there.  Anyone have any insight as to how this works?</span></div><div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Menlo,Monaco,Consolas,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:18px;white-space:pre-wrap;background-color:rgb(245,245,245)\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\